#:culture{:url "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peanut_stew", :id "mli.dish.tigadegue", :kind :dish, :name-local "Tigadèguèna", :country "MLI", :retrieved-at "2026-07-17", :summary "In Mali the Mandinka and Bambara peoples' tigadèguèna variant of peanut stew is traditionally more watery than Senegalese maafe and prepared with unrefined shea butter, served with Malian fufu (tuwo).", :name "Peanut stew", :url-provenance :wikipedia-en}
